WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.700
With me right now is

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.902
somebody who has up front experience

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.870
with Donald Trump

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.804
when he was president

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.739
of the United States,

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.441
and let's call it his

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.542
questionable handling

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.077
of national security information.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.078
The former national security

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.747
adviser, Ambassador John Bolton.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.515
Ambassador Bolton, thanks so much

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.716
for joining us.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.118
First of all, let's just start

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.820
with the basics of the case.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.989
Several members of President Trump's

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:23.790
administration have been

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.026
very critical of his actions

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.660
as described in the indictment.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.228
Former Attorney

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.829
General Bill Barr said, quote,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.498
If even half of it is true, then

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.333
he's toast, unquote.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.501
Do you agree?

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.971
What's your view of this indictment?

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:39.472
Well, I think

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.474
it's a devastating indictment.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.176
It's it's very powerful

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.045
in the way that it's portrayed.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.781
But it's also very narrow, very targeted

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.749
The government didn't throw everything

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.085
and the kitchen sink at the wall.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.787
It has focused this

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.822
and in a way that I think

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.990
as a matter of law

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.725
is going to be very difficult

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.060
for the president to resist.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.762
I think the real question

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.065
is the question of timing and scheduling.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:05.665
You know,

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.567
if Donald Trump were an honest man,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.501
if he were an innocent

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.003
man, he'd be saying,

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.205
I want the trial within 30 days.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:13.907
I want this cloud

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.175
removed from over my head.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.644
I want the stain on my reputation removed

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:18.912
So we'll wait

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.280
and see what Donald Trump does.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.548
I think he'll try and postpone

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.550
it, too, after the 20, 24 election.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.918
So my suggestion

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.752
to Jack Smith

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.220
and the Justice Department

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:27.754
is go

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.590
lean on the Manhattan district attorney

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.759
and get him to move his trial

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.094
until after the election.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.995
This trial should take precedence.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.663
We'll find out

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.697
whether Alvin Bragg

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.200
is a real prosecutor or a political hack.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.770
So there's obviously an historic

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.140
aspect to what we saw today.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.375
A president of the United States

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.144
being arrested and arraigned

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.113
in a federal courthouse.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.614
Looking at it

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.318
through that lens from 30,000 feet.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.252
What was your take?

00:01:59.252 --> 00:01:59.986
What was your

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.055
what did you experience while watching

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.259
I'm sorry.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.594
You were a little bit broken up there.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.962
But but I think it's important

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.662
to understand,

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.464
although this is unprecedented,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.567
to indict a president we have had

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.536
similar kinds of events

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.737
in American history.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.607
Thomas Jefferson, in his second term,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.542
personally ordered the arrest

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.577
and prosecution of Aaron Burr

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.814
for treason, even though Aaron Burr

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.549
had run as Thomas Jefferson's

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.850
vice president.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.819
How did they break apart?

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.887
Wait for it?

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.621
Aaron Burr

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.056
tried to steal the 1800 election

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:37.891
from Jefferson

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.360
by fiddling with the Electoral College.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.461
So, you know,

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.662
we have had a crisis

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.497
involving political figures

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.966
at the highest level of the government.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:47.800
And I don't think

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.103
anybody should think this is necessarily

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.704
an apocalyptic moment.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.673
A lot depends on Donald Trump,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.675
and I think he will do his best

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.210
to make it apocalyptic.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.778
It's depended on the rest of us

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.313
not to let that happen.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.482
You're the former U.S.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.184
ambassador to the United Nations.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:04.951
You were the former

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.086
national security adviser.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.255
You know, of

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.058
classified documents, secret documents.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.860
Do you believe,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.794
based on the facts

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.796
laid out in the indictment,

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.299
that Donald Trump put the U.S.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.367
and its allies at risk

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:25.471
with his possession insecure storage

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.806
and then refusal

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.175
to turn over these documents?

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.543
We also know,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.580
of course, just from reporting

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:34.814
that there have been

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.816
at least two of the two Chinese nationals

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.650
and another con

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.451
woman of sorts

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:41.087
who have gotten access to Mar a Lago.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.323
Now, look,

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:44.924
sorry.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:45.725
Obviously, the

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.260
government has to prove its case

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.495
to a jury. There's no no doubt about it.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.031
But I know what kinds of documents

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.033
we used to give to Donald Trump

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.135
to help him make decisions.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.737
I don't know specifically what

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.372
the documents look like that

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.440
the special counsel

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.442
has listed in the indictment

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.743
But if they're anything like

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.246
some of the things we presented to

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.080
Trump in the Oval

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.615
Office, in the Situation Room

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.650
and the tank at the Pentagon,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.719
it could cause enormous damage,

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.655
incalculable damage to the United States.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.724
And I know some people are saying, well,

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.425
we don't have any allegation.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.194
The Russians have seen these documents

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.396
or the Chinese have seen these documents.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.230
The purpose

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.933
of the provisions of the Espionage Act

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:30.003
and other protections around

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.970
national security

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.573
information is to reduce the chances

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.141
that our adversaries

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.276
can get the documents

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.143
and the behavior

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.545
that's alleged in the complaint.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.781
Intentional, clearly intentional

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.883
after receiving the subpoena

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.386
that Trump didn't want to receive

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:47.820
is just willfully

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.357
puts the United States in grave danger.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.692
I think people need to

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.861
focus on this reality.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:58.331
This is not some case about porn stars

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.532
and hush money.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.402
This the conduct alleged here direct

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.037
threat to the national security

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.772
of the United States.

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.740
One of the big questions

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.575
that I think everybody watching

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:10.810
has is why?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.945
Why would he take these documents

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.380
with him to Mar a Lago?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.582
Why would he show them, as alleged

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.617
in the indictment,

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:20.720
to random people that don't really don't?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.354
Definitely

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.389
don't have national security clearance.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.458
And why would he not just turn them over

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:29.262
when the FBI was demanding that he do so

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.433
Well, I think there's a sense

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.233
of entitlement

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.401
about Donald Trump

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.937
that what he wants, he's entitled to,

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.038
he can take it.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.473
He can do what he wants with it.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.508
And he doesn't face consequences.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.843
And it has to say base

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.978
based on his career to date.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.513
He had very strong reason

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.614
to think he could do

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.717
whatever he wanted to do.

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:52.352
And so he could show to people,

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.487
I've got documents you can't have

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.289
and you can't see.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.790
I can tell the FBI

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.392
that I don't have information

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:00.693
and I can get away with that.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.462
I can do all these things.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:04.764
And his experience would tell him that

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.133
that there would be no downside for him.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.001
Now we're about to find out

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.570
whether there's going to be downside.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.438
I think he's shocked by this.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.172
I think this is

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.241
put he's been put in a

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:15.908
situation

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.244
he has never experienced before.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:18.878
Lastly, sir,

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:19.679
before you go

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.813
and we do appreciate your time,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:21.581
what's your message

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.383
to the Republicans

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.083
who continue

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.418
to stand by his side,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:25.918
the Lindsey

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:26.819
Graham's of the world,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.354
the Marco Rubio's of the world,

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.956
the individuals out there

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:30.456
who are saying

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.458
this is just a political prosecution,

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:33.393
this is not real.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.495
The charges are unfair.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.029
This is just people out

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:37.997
to get Donald Trump.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.432
What would you say to them?

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:40.032
Well,

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.568
yeah, I would say this.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.503
For those who think

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.538
there's a double standard

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.472
and take

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.541
for purposes of this discussion, assume

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.976
there is a double standard, assumed

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:50.576
Hillary Clinton

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:51.811
should have been prosecuted

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.546
and it was not fair that she wasn't

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:55.815
the Joe Biden should be prosecuted.

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.383
And it's not fair that he's not.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.419
That's what these people believe.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.421
The answer to their complaint

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.755
about a double standard,

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:03.356
the question

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.724
they should be asked

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:07.693
is, even though Biden has escaped scot

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.196
free, Clinton has escaped scot free,

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:11.164
fill in the blank,

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:11.798
has escaped

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:12.832
scot free,

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:14.934
is the answer to the double standard

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.369
to let Donald Trump

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:17.403
escape scot free

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.472
is the answer to the double standard

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.541
to revert to no standard at all.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:22.809
I think that's wrong.

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.877
I think Republicans have rightly believed

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.312
for a long time

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.548
that when you don't prosecute criminals,

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.283
you get more crimes.

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.284
And the answer is,

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:33.152
when you've got the allegations

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:34.353
in a complaint like this

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.254
with the conduct

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.757
that that that the indictment shows

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:40.460
the prosecution is entirely warranted,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.695
worry about the others later.

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:44.697
This is a decision before you.

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:46.732
I want Republicans who think Trump

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.501
should be given a pass to say

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.837
so explicitly, don't. What about it?

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.505
Talk about whether you think

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:54.307
this complaint, this indictment

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.808
shows criminal behavior.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:56.676
And if it does,

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.845
we should all favor prosecuting.

00:07:58.845 --> 00:07:59.145
All right.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.213
Former ambassador

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.380
and national security adviser

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:01.848
John Bolton,

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:02.982
thank you so much for your time at.

